+# Paired rank and generalized first-action boundary
+
+Claim type: bounded_theorem
+
+**Status: conditional-support.** This source package records the supplied native infinite reference and exact midpoint family. Independent selected-matrix replay is complete. Independent generalized saved-stage replay is also accepted; final canonical review is recorded separately in the packet.
+
+The [compression/action boundary](NATIVE_COMPRESSION_ACTION_BOUNDARY_NOTE_2026-09-09.md) fixes the five original ordered24 paired selections. ORIGINAL has399 raw/798 closed columns; DATA adds three bare sources, giving402/804. Trial vectors remain in ORIGINAL. Rational midpoint poles and alpha define the same family throughout, with outward square roots and separate physical scalar uncertainty. No reselected subspace or exact Gauss-root substitution is made.
+
+## Positive paired rank without a narrow coefficient box
+
+Let S contain the ordered48 columns (s1,Gamma s1,...,s24,Gamma s24), and let T be the saved exact positive upper triangular dyadic candidate. Write W=ST and H=W*W. Direct selected-Gram enclosures establish ||H−I||<=e<8/10^6 in all five orbits. Hence H is positive definite, W and S have full paired column rank, and the exact isometry V=W H^(-1/2) has exactly their span. Independence of only the24 unpaired vectors would not suffice.
+
+The separate coefficient enclosure in the original ordered triangular gauge passes its l1 gate but fails its full-width gate in every orbit. This does not negate the rank certificate. Conversely, rank alone gives no small action leakage. The original proof and exact saved selected root/POST records are imported in the packet, including the distinction between polar isometry and the ordered triangular frame.
+
+## Generalized leakage certificate
+
+For either actual impurity K_A, define A=W*K_A W and Z=(K_A W)*(K_A W), so A is real skew and
+
+\[
+N=Z+A H^{-1}A=(K_AW)^*(I-VV^*)K_AW\succeq0.
+\]
+
+An exact symmetric candidate X supplies an inverse residual bound epsilon=||I−HX||/(1−e). Thus replacing H^-1 by X perturbs the Schur matrix by at most ||A||^2 epsilon. Combining this with the interval-matrix radius q yields a verified center N0±q. Gershgorin gives an upper bound divided by1−e. Each diagonal gives the lower bound
+
+\[
+\delta_A^2=\|(I-VV^*)K_AV\|^2\ge
+\max_i\frac{\max(0,(N_0)_{ii}-q)}{(H_{ii})_{upper}}.
+\]
+
+The exact proof and implementation keep the physical rank-two impurity action; it is not commuted through Gamma. DATA supplies first action only. No action on newly appended DATA vectors is inferred.
+
+For all five fixed trial spaces and both impurities, the computed rational lower bound exceeds53/100 in h=1 units. Consequently the proposed squared target10^-12 is excluded for these trial spaces. Restoring units gives delta_A^2>(53/100)h^2. This excludes the target itself for these particular spans, rather than merely saying an upper-bound test failed. It does not prove failure of other trial spaces, a model impossibility, or accuracy of any dynamics approximation.
+
+## Evidence and limits
+
+Selected principal production and its independent full-matrix saved check are accepted; all five coefficient-width gates remain false. Generalized production completed once in20.61 external seconds, with108183552 bytes sampled whole-tree peak. Its root validates retained structure and scalar inequalities but does not independently reproduce every matrix contraction. The independent saved-stage replay reproduced all5286 original stages across five orbits, retaining10588 independent files in32.12 external seconds with120569856 bytes sampled whole-tree peak. Raw native interval truth remains inherited.
+
+The compact standard-library runner checks exact summary inequalities, original orbit copies, POST receipt bindings and a two-dimensional Schur identity. It does not load or replay the archived native matrices. The recovery map identifies committed blobs for every scientific input pin. Platform runtime files are separately declared external requirements. The compact package does not bundle or re-execute the full matrix replay. No phase, bulk gap, node form factor, full sixth-order coefficient, or propagation accuracy is claimed.
